{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VPD5xscUmzvxKtrSCvvVV2","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\\section*{Ethics Statement}\n2\t\\label{sec:ethics}\n3\t\n4\tAll texts analyzed in this work are LLM-generated from publicly available Wikipedia seeds; no personal or sensitive data is involved.\n5\tOur method estimates the generation depth of a text passage (how many recursive generation steps it has undergone), not the identity of its author.\n6\tIndividual authorship attribution is outside both the scope and the capability of this approach; privacy implications are minimal.\n7\tWe acknowledge that depth estimation tools could in principle be used to selectively suppress machine-generated text in contexts where such content is legitimate (e.g., accessibility tools, assistive writing).\n8\tWe encourage deployment in data governance pipelines where provenance transparency, rather than content removal, is the objective.\n9\tAll code, data, and trained models will be released upon publication.\n10\t\n11\t\\paragraph{Licenses.}\n12\tAll generator models are publicly available under permissive licenses (Apache 2.0 for Pythia, OLMo, and Mistral; Qwen License for Qwen3; Llama Community License for Llama 3.2).\n13\tWikipedia seed passages are distributed under CC BY-SA 3.0.\n14\t\n15\t\\paragraph{Compute budget.}\n16\tAll experiments were conducted on 4$\\times$ NVIDIA RTX 5090 GPUs (32\\,GB each), totaling approximately 62 GPU-hours.\n17\t\n18\t\\paragraph{Software.}\n19\tExperiments used Python 3.12.3, PyTorch 2.10.0 (CUDA 12.8), Transformers 4.57.6, XGBoost 3.2.0, scikit-learn 1.8.0, NumPy 2.2.6, pandas 3.0.2, and SciPy 1.17.1.\n20\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Aa4LbC8tVN8tPubtpYmsUq","session_id":"d4cded27-964c-4711-9220-b05f8309dff9","uuid":"9b62dd47-62a0-4a7a-9eb9-bec85b17da1c","timestamp":"2026-05-20T10:44:55.266Z"}
